<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

Its easy to create many variations of the &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Slider&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control using &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Visuals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.
They have minimum and maximum values that can be specified per control, and also a step amount.
Here are a few possible styles:

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Progress Bar&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; controls are similar, except they cannot be interacted with by the user... although they can be animated.
</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
